@.str.439 = private unnamed_addr constant [1966 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Show what packages are installed in the default profile:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix profile list\0A  Name:               gdb\0A  Flake attribute:    legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.gdb\0A  Original flake URL: flake:nixpkgs\0A  Locked flake URL:   github:NixOS/nixpkgs/7b38b03d76ab71bdc8dc325e3f6338d984cc35ca\0A  Store paths:        /nix/store/indzcw5wvlhx6vwk7k4iq29q15chvr3d-gdb-11.1\0A\0A  Name:               blender-bin\0A  Flake attribute:    packages.x86_64-linux.default\0A  Original flake URL: flake:blender-bin\0A  Locked flake URL:   github:edolstra/nix-warez/91f2ffee657bf834e4475865ae336e2379282d34?dir=blender\0A  Store paths:        /nix/store/i798sxl3j40wpdi1rgf391id1b5klw7g-blender-bin-3.1.2\0A  ```\0A\0A  Note that you can unambiguously rebuild a package from a profile\0A  through its locked flake URL and flake attribute, e.g.\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build github:edolstra/nix-warez/91f2ffee657bf834e4475865ae336e2379282d34?dir=blender#packages.x86_64-linux.default\0A  ```\0A\0A  will build the package `blender-bin` shown above.\0A\0A# Description\0A\0AThis command shows what packages are currently installed in a\0Aprofile. For each installed package, it shows the following\0Ainformation:\0A\0A* `Name`: A unique name used to unambiguously identify the\0A  package in invocations of `nix profile remove` and `nix profile\0A  upgrade`.\0A\0A* `Index`: An integer that can be used to unambiguously identify the\0A  package in invocations of `nix profile remove` and `nix profile upgrade`.\0A  (*Deprecated, will be removed in a future version in favor of `Name`.*)\0A\0A* `Flake attribute`: The flake output attribute path that provides the\0A  package (e.g. `packages.x86_64-linux.hello`).\0A\0A* `Original flake URL`: The original (\22unlocked\22) flake reference\0A  specified by the user when the package was first installed via `nix\0A  profile install`.\0A\0A* `Locked flake URL`: The locked flake reference to which the original\0A  flake reference was resolved.\0A\0A* `Store paths`: The store path(s) of the package.\0A\0A\00", align 1
