@.str.471 = private unnamed_addr constant [41 x i8] c"delete non-current versions of a profile\00", align 1
@.str.472 = private unnamed_addr constant [495 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Delete all versions of the default profile older than 100 days:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix profile wipe-history --profile /tmp/profile --older-than 100d\0A  removing profile version 515\0A  removing profile version 514\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0AThis command deletes non-current versions of a profile, making it\0Aimpossible to roll back to these versions. By default, all non-current\0Aversions are deleted. With `--older-than` *N*`d`, all non-current\0Aversions older than *N* days are deleted.\0A\0A\00", align 1
